> you're not really you anymore.
>
> Why pets would still be tame after that is another matter.

That can't be the way polymorph works, for the following reasons:

1. If you poly into a Xorn and your brain's left intact, a human brain
is still as incapable of phasing through walls as is a human hand/leg/
anything else. If you poly into an amorphous creature and your brain
was left intact, it would instantly drop to the floor and be left
behind whenever you moved. If you poly into a rock golem and your
brain remains flesh, *it* would still turn to stone when you "hear the
cockatrice's hissing", killing you. Etc ad nauseum.

2. When you poly into a foo, you take on the mental attributes of the
foo as well as the physical ones - wisdom and intelligence.

So it seems that when you polymorph, you really DO become the thing
you polymorph into, brain and all.

If you had said "if you're magically changed into a slime, your will/
personality is left intact," that might be a better argument. But it's
obvious from the above examples that will/personality does NOT reside
in the brain in the Nethack universe, but rather in a "soul" or other
insubstantial location. (As a further example, when you die and come
back as a ghost, the ghost retains its personality and will (after
all, it goes on guarding its possessions.) It doesn't have any brain
at all. Neither do shades and wraiths, but they can still make
decisions and act in a reasonably intelligent manner.)
So, agreed, your brain might be "destroyed" (changed to slime) by a
sliming, but no more so then when you polymorph into the slime
voluntarily, and since brain does not equal mind in the Nethack
universe, it shouldn't affect your will or identity at all.

